# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MedGuard (Triage One) — .gitignore
#
# GOLDEN RULE: raw MIMIC data, licensed dataset files, secrets and generated
# model artifacts must NEVER be committed to this repository or pushed to
# GitHub. MIMIC-IV-ED is licensed under the ODC Open Database License (ODbL)
# and the PhysioNet Credentialed Health Data License.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Licensed research datasets (NEVER COMMIT) -----------------------------
# Raw MIMIC-IV-ED demo / full dataset files.
mimic-iv-ed-demo-2.2/
mimic-iv-ed-demo-2.2.zip
mimic-iv-ed-*/
# The Triagegeist synthetic dataset. It is redistributed under third-party
# terms, so it is obtained separately (see docs/DEPLOYMENT_FIX.md) rather than
# committed here. Only the aggregate reports derived from it are tracked.
triagegeist/
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.gz
*.bz2
*.xz
*.7z

# Any other private / licensed dataset location and generated
# patient-level exports of research data.
data/
datasets/
raw_data/
private/
exports/
*_patient_level*.csv
*_patient_level*.json

# Generated (non-source) copies of processed research data.
data/processed/
data/interim/
data/raw/

# Pipeline output derived from the research data. Regenerate the aggregate
# artifacts with `venv/bin/python -m backend.ml.build_reports` and
# `venv/bin/python -m backend.ml.run_data_prep`.
reports/

